4. Tina (Apache License 2.0) -- design followed, no source copied

   Gina is a Go port of the concurrency model of pmbanugo/tina
   (https://github.com/pmbanugo/tina): thread-per-core shards, isolates, effects,
   fixed-size messages, SPSC rings, supervision. SPEC.md records that it was
   reimplemented from the documented behaviour. No Tina source is copied. If any
   is, Tina's Apache-2.0 license and NOTICE must be added here and the changes
   marked.


5. Specifications

   The protocols are implemented from their specifications: PostgreSQL's
   frontend/backend protocol, TLS 1.3 (RFC 8446), HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2 (RFC 9112,
   9113), HPACK (RFC 7541, whose Appendix B Huffman table generated
   extensions/http2/huffman_table.go), WebSocket (RFC 6455, 8441), Web Push
   (RFC 8030, 8291, 8292) and SCRAM (RFC 5802, 7677). No specification text or
   third-party implementation is included.
